message: "Please cite the technical report and the archived repository release."
title: "Seven-Word Subcore Exclusions and a Six-Hole Plateau in the Ternary Covering Problem K_3(7,3)"
type: software
abstract: "A reproducible scoped theorem for the unresolved ternary covering number K_3(7,3). For each of eight seven-word subcores obtained from an explicit eight-word core, every set of at most four added centers leaves at least six radius-3 holes, and equality is attained. Consequently, no size-at-most-11 covering code contains any of these subcores or an isometric copy. Independent Rust and C++20 implementations verify the four deletion-orbit representatives. The global interval 11 <= K_3(7,3) <= 12 remains unchanged."
